      "message": "I\u0027d lean toward dropping the \"Co-Authored-By: Claude\" footer — but as one maintainer, not as a ruling. This isn\u0027t mine to decide, and I\u0027m not on the ESC or a community manager.\n\nMy reasoning: the code was authored by you. A tool that helped you write it isn\u0027t a contributor in the sense our process recognizes — a contribution is tied to the person who certifies its origin [1], and an AI can\u0027t be that party. I\u0027m also not aware of any official Gerrit Code Review policy that endorses such a footer.\n\nSince we have no project-wide rule (yet), I\u0027d defer the actual decision to the ESC and the community managers. I\u0027m happy to open an issue so they can discuss it and set a policy; in the meantime I\u0027d suggest removing it here.\n\n[1]: https://cla.developers.google.com/clas",
